  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There are multiple parts to this bug:\n- You must be spawning an object that exists in the scene and is not a prefab. \n- The object being spawned has multiple object sync components within it.\n- The method to spawn the object is \"initiated\" through a UI Button with an animation calling it's Press method. \nIf all the conditions are met, the spawned object will never sync. Spawning this same object through other methods will result in it syncing properly. \nExample world:\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_1f525a94-39d5-440d-a9ac-85f0fd9d4723\nThere are three methods to spawn an object:\n- Directly from OnInteract\n- Using a UI button pressed by the player\n- Using a UI button and an animation to call Press()\nThe first two will spawn objects that sync. The last one will spawn an object that always fails to sync.\nPublished world that exhibits the issue:\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_1f525a94-39d5-440d-a9ac-85f0fd9d4723\nMain mechanics rely on the world being synced. Now it only works for Master as other users can't initiate proper triggers without objects being synced.",
